Mantik
======

This project includes software derived from third-party open source.

WPILib / controls_js_sim
--------------------------

PID simulation physics in `src/lib/pid-sim/physics/` is ported from the
WPILib documentation interactive controls examples (controls_js_sim), which are
part of the WPILib project.

  - Source: https://github.com/wpilibsuite/wpilib-docs/tree/main/source/_extensions/controls_js_sim
  - WPILib: https://github.com/wpilibsuite/allwpilib
  - License: BSD-3-Clause (see WPILib and wpilib-docs repositories)

Motor constant patterns in `src/lib/pid-sim/physics/dcMotor.ts` follow
`edu.wpi.first.math.system.plant.DCMotor` from WPILib.

Trapezoid profile and related utilities reference WPILib Java implementations.

When you redistribute Mantik, retain this notice along with `LICENSE`.

Java Playground (in-browser runner)
-----------------------------------

The Java lesson runner in `src/lib/java-playground/` and `src/components/java-playground/`
is derived from community Mantik forks (including work by FRC 4451 and FRC 3476) and
uses [CheerpJ](https://cheerpj.com) (Leaning Technologies) for a browser JVM, plus
Eclipse ECJ for in-browser compilation.

  - CheerpJ: https://cheerpj.com — see Leaning Technologies license terms for production use
  - ECJ: Eclipse Public License 2.0 (downloaded at build time into `public/java-playground/`)
